WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:03.300
Doctor Strange is undeniably fun from start
to finish.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:07.660
By introducing the mystic arts, the multiverse,
and a whole lot of Dormammu, the Benedict

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:12.420
Cumberbatch-starring superhero sorcery story
keeps Marvel Studios' streak alive into the

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.910
latter half of 2016.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.430
But it's not perfect.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:20.620
Call us nitpickers, call us buzzkills, call
us acolytes of the dark dimension, but we're

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.280
about to dive into some of the less magical
aspects of Doctor Strange's plot.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.750
While its story is actually really tight overall,
there are still a few niggling plot holes

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.970
and contrivances that you can't simply wave
away with the Wand of Watoomb...

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.210
"Teach me!"

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.010
...no matter how hard you try.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:41.340
Oh, and it should go without saying, but let's
say the magic words anyway: massive spoilers

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.990
ahead.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.350
Insecurity system

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.920
The movie begins with Kaecilius, played by
Mads Mikkelsen, breaking into the Ancient

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.899
One's library to steal a couple of pages from
one of her very favorite books.

00:00:52.899 --> 00:00:56.809
These books contain the most advanced knowledge
and spells in the Ancient One's possession.

00:00:56.809 --> 00:00:57.950
They're pretty important!

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:02.379
That must be why she keeps them loosely draped
in chains that appear to be entirely decorative.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:06.469
It goes without saying that Kaecilius needs
to steal the pages describing the ritual for

00:01:06.469 --> 00:01:10.759
the movie to, y'know, actually happen, it
wouldn't have taken much more on the movie's

00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:14.689
part to make it a little harder for the bad
guy to actually steal them.

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:18.469
And hey, while we're on that subject, why
didn't Kaecilius just take the whole book?

00:01:18.469 --> 00:01:22.649
Of course, if that happened, then the book
wouldn't be incredibly easy for our hero,

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.929
Doctor Strange, to take a look at when he
needed to learn about the rituals later in

00:01:25.929 --> 00:01:26.959
the movie.

00:01:26.959 --> 00:01:28.079
Speaking of which…

00:01:28.079 --> 00:01:29.679
Oh, hey, Kaecilius

00:01:29.679 --> 00:01:34.810
Isn't it weird that, on the night that Strange
wanders into the magic library, when he reads

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:38.880
from the book with the missing ritual pages
stolen by Kaecilius, when he teaches himself

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.149
how to use the all-powerful Eye of Agamotto
that can manipulate time itself … that's

00:01:43.149 --> 00:01:47.549
the very night — the very moment — when
the villain decides to launch his attack on

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:51.219
all three magical sanctums, including the
library itself.

00:01:51.219 --> 00:01:55.241
Not only that, but it also happens literally
seconds after Doctor Strange says that he

00:01:55.241 --> 00:01:58.579
won't be "dragged into some sort of mystical
war!"

00:01:58.579 --> 00:02:00.029
That's bad timing, Doc.

00:02:00.029 --> 00:02:01.509
Next time, why don't you try saying,

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:04.239
"I've got a bad feeling about this"

00:02:04.239 --> 00:02:05.239
Or maybe…

00:02:05.239 --> 00:02:08.239
"I don't know how much more I can take."

00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:09.239
"Aahhh!"

00:02:09.239 --> 00:02:12.560
Those words, too, must be powerful spells
that magically compel the plot to move forward

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.390
at the most dramatic moment.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:17.110
Eye, oh my...

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:20.560
While we're on the subject of that scene in
the library, Wong and Mordo both seem pretty

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.140
unhappy about how Strange went and started
messing with the Eye of Agamotto.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.750
The two tell him about all the terrible consequences
that could come from monkeying with the timestream,

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.310
and then they put the book back.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:34.580
Just one thing, though: why didn't they take
that big honkin' amulet off of him, too?

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:39.860
Oh, it's so he can have it during the villain
fight that's about to take place for the rest

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:40.860
of the movie?

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:41.860
Oh, okay.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:42.860
That's cool.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:43.860
No time to explain

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.840
We hear a vague list of consequences that
the world might possibly face as a result

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.460
of Strange's experiments with the Eye, like
time loops and alternate timelines or something

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:53.640
equally unspecified.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:57.150
And, hey: we all saw Back to the Future Part
II.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:03.370
Nobody wants Biff Tannen to take over the
world and get down with our moms.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.620
"Noooooo!"

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.320
But aside from the time loops that were admittedly
part of the extremely clever and satisfying

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:15.040
climactic battle with Dormammu, we never actually
learn anything concrete about the dangers

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.040
of screwing with time.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.930
It kind of seems like there might be no actual
consequences at all, despite Mordo thinking

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:25.490
that they're dire enough to leave the good
guys and become a supervillain by the end.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:29.440
But what was really so very bad about using
the Eye to save the entire planet from being

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.240
sucked into the Dark Dimension?

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:34.680
Kung fu cloak

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.420
Remember that wacky magic carpet from Aladdin?

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:42.630
The one that was so expressive and fun, despite
not having a mouth or eyes or even a face?

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:45.110
Well, that carpet's back — in cloak form.

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:49.060
That's right, the Cloak of Levitation is the
magical item that takes a liking to the good

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:53.010
doctor and helps him in his battle against
Kaecilius and his goons in the New York sanctum.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.400
It's pretty handy.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.130
Except … when it isn't, like when Doctor
Strange gets stabbed in the chest.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.760
And literally any other time after its initial
introduction.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.209
The cloak seems to have a mind of its own
and acts as an important ally for Strange

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:07.190
on his heroic quest — but only when it's
convenient.

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:10.010
Otherwise, it's just, y'know, a cape.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:11.600
But a fancy-looking cape!

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.490
Two sanctums, or three?

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:17.630
We learn from Wong that there are three sanctums
protecting the world from evil.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:21.609
Kaecilius and his minions take down the one
in London, and destroy the one in Hong Kong.

00:04:21.609 --> 00:04:24.650
And that's when Dormammu's Dark dimension
starts to come through.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:27.690
But the New York sanctum is still standing.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:31.219
So how many of these things does the world
actually need?

00:04:31.219 --> 00:04:33.449
Follow-up appointment

00:04:33.449 --> 00:04:37.469
Regardless of whatever plot holes or hiccups
we think we may have found here, Doctor Strange

00:04:37.469 --> 00:04:38.999
was hugely fun.

00:04:38.999 --> 00:04:42.850
When it comes to an amazing introduction to
the weird, magical side of the Marvel Cinematic

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:46.729
Universe, one thing's for sure: the Doctor
is in.

00:04:46.729 --> 00:04:48.349
Thanks for watching!

